  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 153 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nA very stout upper-level ridge will build across the area this \nweekend and then linger through next week. The lack of strong \nsurface flow/moisture advection northward from the Gulf will keep \ndewpoints from getting too out of hand (in the upper 60s to around \n70). Transpiration will be a bit lower as well with harvest ramping \nup across the area. However, temperatures will increase to the mid \nto upper 90s! There is a 50-80% chance that temperatures will exceed \n95 degree by Monday afternoon, but that increases to a 70-90% chance \nby Wednesday. Heat index values will increase to 100-105 degrees \nthrough much of the week, with the probabilities of heat index \nvalues exceeding 100 reaching the 50-70% range by Wednesday. Major \nto extreme heat risks will is expected to develop from Tuesday \nthrough the rest of next week.\n\nThis will be a dangerous and prolonged heat event for the area with \nsome of the hottest temperatures experience over the summer. Record \nhigh temperatures are not anticipated; however, multiple record \nminimum temperatures could be observed from Tuesday through at least \nFriday with lows staying in the mid 70s!!\n\nNo major cool downs are in sight through this forecast issuance.",
